Author-Name: Denuit, Michel
Author-Workplace-Name: Université catholique de Louvain, LIDAM/ISBA, Belgium
Author-Name: Trufin, Julien
Author-Workplace-Name: Université Libre de Bruxelles
Title: Generalization error for Tweedie models: decomposition and error reduction with bagging
Abstract: Wüthrich and Buser (DOI:10.2139/ssrn.2870308, 2020) studied the generalization error for Poisson regression models. This short note aims to extend their results to the Tweedie family of distributions, to which the Poisson law belongs. In case of bagging, a new condition emerges that becomes increasingly binding with the power parameter involved in the Tweedie variance function.
Keywords: Generalization error ; Supervised learning ; Exponential dispersion family ; Tweedie ; Bagging
Note: In: European Actuarial Journal, 2021, vol. 11, p. 325-331
Length: 7
Series: UCLouvain, LIDAM, ISBA
