Number: 2021046
Creation-Date: 2021-09-06
DOI: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.insmatheco.2021.08.013
Handle: RePEc:aiz:louvar:2021046

Template-Type: ReDIF-Paper 1.0
Author-Name: Hanna, Vanessa
Author-Workplace-Name: Université catholique de Louvain, LIDAM/ISBA, Belgium
Author-Name: Hieber, Peter
Author-Workplace-Name: Université catholique de Louvain, LIDAM/ISBA, Belgium
Author-Name: Devolder, Pierre
Author-Workplace-Name: Université catholique de Louvain, LIDAM/ISBA, Belgium
Title: Mixed participating and unit-linked life insurance contracts: design, pricing and optimal strategy
Abstract: In many countries, the decline in interest rates has reduced the interest in traditional participating life insurance contracts with investment guarantees and has led to a shift to unit-linked policies without guarantees. We design a novel mixed insurance contract splitting premium payments between a participating and a unit-linked fund. An additional guarantee fee is applied on the unit-linked return in order to increase the investment guarantee of the participating fund. In a utility-based framework, using power utility and prospect theory as preference functions, we show that the mixed product is usually perceived more attractive than a full investment in either the unit-linked or the participating contract. The guarantee fee is beneficial for conservative investors interested in stronger protection against losses. This is also interesting from a marketing perspective: By the increase of the guarantee in the participating product, zero or negative guaranteed rates can be avoided.
Keywords: Life and pension insurance ; participating contract ; unit-linked contract ; investment guarantee ; mixed insurance contracts ; expected utility ; cumulative prospect theory
Note: In: Scandinavian Actuarial Journal, 2021
Length: 26
Series: UCLouvain, LIDAM, ISBA
Number: 2021047
Creation-Date: 2021-10-28
DOI: https://doi.org/10.1080/03461238.2021.1992001
